  {
   "qno": 15,
   "question_id": null,
   "question_type": null,
   "subject": null,
   "section": null,
   "segment": 1,
   "text": "NOT",
   "options": {
    "A": "$\\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{2}$",
    "B": "$\\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{4}$",
    "C": "$\\frac{3}{2 \\sqrt{3}}$",
    "D": "$\\frac{3}{4 \\sqrt{3}}$\n\nOfficial Ans. by NTA (B)\nAns. (B)\n\nSol. $\\mathrm{C}:(\\mathrm{x}-2)^{2}+\\mathrm{y}^{2}=1$\n\nEquation of chord $\\mathrm{AB}: 2 \\mathrm{x}=3$\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\n\\mathrm{OA}=\\mathrm{OB}=\\sqrt{3} \\\\\n\\mathrm{AM}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n\\end{array}$$\n\nArea of triangle $\\mathrm{OAB}=\\frac{1}{2}(2 \\mathrm{AM})(\\mathrm{OM})$\n$$=\\frac{3 \\sqrt{3}}{4} \\text { sq. units }$$\n14. Let the hyperbola $\\mathrm{H}: \\frac{\\mathrm{x}^{2}}{\\mathrm{a}^{2}}-\\frac{\\mathrm{y}^{2}}{\\mathrm{~b}^{2}}=1$ pass through the point $(2 \\sqrt{2},-2 \\sqrt{2})$. A parabola is drawn whose focus is same as the focus of H with positive abscissa and the directrix of the parabola passes through the other focus of H. If the length of the latus rectum of the parabola is e times the length of the latus rectum of H , where e is the eccentricity of H, then which of the following points lies on the parabola?\n(A) $(2 \\sqrt{3}, 3 \\sqrt{2})$\n(B) $(3 \\sqrt{3},-6 \\sqrt{2})$\n(C) $(\\sqrt{3},-\\sqrt{6})$\n(D) $(3 \\sqrt{6}, 6 \\sqrt{2})$\n\nOfficial Ans. by NTA (B)\nAns. (B)\nSol. $\\mathrm{H}: \\frac{\\mathrm{x}^{2}}{\\mathrm{a}^{2}}-\\frac{\\mathrm{y}^{2}}{\\mathrm{~b}^{2}}=1$\nFoci : S (ae, 0), S' (-ae, 0)\nFoot of directrix of parabola is (-ae, 0)\nFocus of parabola is $(\\mathrm{ae}, 0)$\nNow, semi latus rectum of parabola $=\\left|\\mathrm{SS}^{\\prime}\\right|=2 \\mathrm{ae}$\nGiven, $4 \\mathrm{ae}=\\mathrm{e}\\left(\\frac{2 \\mathrm{~b}^{2}}{\\mathrm{a}}\\right)$\n$$\\Rightarrow b^{2}=2 a^{2}$$\n\nGiven, $(2 \\sqrt{2},-2 \\sqrt{2})$ lies on H\n$$\\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{\\mathrm{a}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{~b}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{8}$$\n\nFrom (1) and (2)\n$$\\begin{array}{l}\na^{2}=4, b^{2}=8 \\\\\n\\because b^{2}=a^{2}\\left(e^{2}-1\\right) \\\\\n\\therefore e=\\sqrt{3}\n\\end{array}$$\n\n⇒ Equation of parabola is $\\mathrm{y}^{2}=8 \\sqrt{3} \\mathrm{x}$\n\nJEE Exam Solution\nwww.esaral.com\n4"
   },
